"Brutes are the physical class, with few spells and tightly focused skills."
"Their focus leaves them little versatility."
"An S-rank Brute is a titan; a C-rank Brute is middling."
"Arjun Thomas is an S-rank Brute focused almost purely on physical strength."
"Brutes are about 30% of the chosen, the most of any class, and the most traded."
"Brute subtypes include Longsight, Morph, Speedster, Agility, strength-type and Audial."
"Audial Brutes are held able to overhear things and even to cure tinnitus."
"Brutes get many foundational points."
"Brute types include vocal Brutes, who may perform opera for off-island jobs."
"Combat-class C-ranks are rarely summoned, mostly for appearances."
"Brute powers are body modifications; Flail Brutes elongate limbs but get no full shapeshifting."
"Dura Brute is an unofficial Strength-Stamina hybrid made through System micro-tweaks."
"Morph Brutes can shift between big and strong or little and fast in seconds."
"Most Brutes cannot take narrow point damage at top speed."
"Aquatic Brutes, an uncommon enviro type, breathe underwater and endure pressure and temperature."
"Arts schools have tried for thirty years to define a Dancer or Graceful Brute subclass."
"The System is loosening about letting Brutes hybridize in new ways past low levels."
"Orator Brutes exist among the vocal types."
"New Speed Brutes are almost all foundation points, the System withholding active skills at first."
"Instructor-level Brutes may still gain two or three levels a year."
